OCOMP  -  COMPARE & DUMP FILES UNDER A MASK    1978 APRIL 3  T.C.

DEFAULT OUTPUT IS TO TTY:	DEFAULT OUTPUT EXTENSION IS .LS
THE MASK IS SPECIFIED AS THE LEAST SIGNIFICANT 12 BITS OF '=N'.

1) COMPARE:
	TWO INPUT FILES ARE COMPARED UNDER A MASK.  IF SECOND IN-
	PUT DEVICE IS SPECIFIED WITH NO FILENAME, THE FIRST INPUT
	FILENAME IS REUSED.  IF MASK=0, 7777 IS USED.

2) DUMP:
	ONE INPUT FILE.  DUMP ALL WORDS WITH NO MASK BITS OFF.
	IF MASK=0, 7777 IS USED.

3) SEARCH:
	ONE INPUT FILE WITH /S; DUMP ALL WORDS EQUAL TO THE MASK.


THE COMMAND DECODER IS RECALLED AFTER THE SPECIFIED OPERATIONS ARE
COMPLETED UNLESS INPUT WAS TERMINATED BY AN 'ESCAPE' OR 'ALTMODE'.

OTHER COMMAND DECODER OPTIONS:

/I   IMAGE MODE
	INPUT FILE IS CORE IMAGE (SAVE) FILE.  DEFAULT INPUT EX-
	TENSION IS .SV.  ADDRESSING IS BY MEMORY ADDRESS, RATHER
	THAN BY FILE ADDRESS.
/C  CCB OUTPUT
	WHEN COMBINED WITH /I, CCB IS PRINTED AS PART OF THE RUN
	TITLE.

/D  DIFFERENCE MODE
	ONLY OUTPUT IS A MESSAGE TELLING THAT FILES COMPARED ARE
	SAME OR DIFFERENT.

/F  FORM FEED
	ALL BLOCKS WHICH CAUSE OUTPUT HAVE THEIR OUTPUT PRECEEDED
	BY A FORM FEED CHARACTER.

/T  TELETYPE
	OUTPUT FORMAT IS NARROWED FOR OUTPUT TO 72 COLUMN DEVICES
	SUCH AS TELETYPES OR VIDEO TERMINALS.

/H  HEADER
	OUTPUT HEADER LINE EVEN IF OUTPUT DEVICE IS TTY:.


ERRORS ARE INDICATED BY A "USER ERROR ..." MESSAGE.  THE PROGRAM
IS NOT RESTARTABLE.

ERROR		CONDITION
  1	MORE THAN TWO INPUT FILES
  2	OUTPUT FILE TOO SMALL
  3	OUTPUT HANDLER FETCH OR ENTER FAILED
  4	INPUT HANDLER FETCH OR LOOKUP FAILED
  5	INPUT FILE #1 ERROR
  6	INPUT FILE #2 ERROR
  7	OUTPUT FILE ERROR
  8	OUTPUT FILE CLOSE FAILED
  9	CCB DECODE ERROR
